  "body": "The maintainer reported this in chat on 2026-11-15, on the v0.21.0 tree.\n\nWhat happens: the viewport draws the machine work envelope (#1567, the Browser checkbox) with its Z centre on the worktable plane. Half of the box is below the table.\n\nExpected: the envelope starts on the top of the worktable and goes up. Its bottom face is on the table plane. The box then shows where a point is in the machine space.\n\nThe maintainer's words: \"the work envelope is not sitting on the \"plane\" instead its centering around it. Which would not help when estimating where something is in the 3D space... As the work envelope begins ontop of the worktable . and not half way below it.\"\n\nQuestions for the work:\n\n- Find where the envelope box gets its Z range. Find if X and Y have the same centre error against the table.\n- Find if a travel-limit or reach check uses the same box (`crates/post/src/machine/envelope.rs`). If a check uses it, the defect is under the safety floor: raise the effort label to `effort:high` and say so here.\n- Name the machine file and the setup that the reading uses.\n\nDone means:\n\n- The bottom face of the drawn envelope is on the worktable plane for each machine file that has travel limits.\n- A test pins the Z range of the envelope against the table plane (a structural or value test, not a pixel snapshot).\n- A comment here says if a check used the wrong box, with the result.\n",
